.TH PATH_IS_SEPARATOR 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
path_is_separator \- Check if a character is a directory separator

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/path_internal.h>

.IB int
.IB path_is_separator(const char* c);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpath_is_separator\fR function checks if a given character is recognized as a directory separator. It uses the \fBpath_issep\fR function to perform the check.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB c
The character to be checked.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 1 if the character is a directory separator, and 0 otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBpath_is_separator\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/path_internal.h>

int main() {
    const char* c = "/";
    int is_sep = path_is_separator(c);
    printf("Is separator: %d\n", is_sep);
    return 0;
}
.nef